mink-optee-client for Debian
=============================

Overview
--------
This package provides a Qualcomm-adapted build of the upstream OP-TEE PKCS#11
TEE client library (libckqteec), designed to communicate with the Qualcomm
Trusted Execution Environment (QTEE) via the MinkIPC transport layer.

It is based on the upstream OP-TEE Client source (https://github.com/OP-TEE/optee_client)
at version 4.0.0, with minimal patches applied to link against the Qualcomm
MinkIPC stack (libminkteec, libminkadaptor) instead of the standard OP-TEE transport.

Relationship to optee-client
-----------------------------
This package is NOT a replacement for the upstream optee-client package. The
two packages are designed to work with different TEE stacks and firmware:

  - optee-client  : targets the upstream OP-TEE firmware stack.
  - mink-optee-client : targets the Qualcomm QTEE firmware stack via MinkIPC.

The libraries shipped by each package have distinct SONAMEs and do not
conflict at the binary level:

  - optee-client ships      : libckteec.so.0
  - mink-optee-client ships : libckqteec.so.0

However, the development package (mink-optee-client-dev) ships header files
(e.g. pkcs11.h) that overlap with those provided by optee-client-dev.
Therefore, mink-optee-client-dev and optee-client-dev cannot be installed
simultaneously. See the "Development Files" section below.

Packages
--------

libckqteec0
 The shared runtime library (libckqteec.so.0) used by applications that
 communicate with the Qualcomm QTEE via the PKCS#11 interface over MinkIPC.
 This is the package end-users and runtime dependencies should pull in.

mink-optee-client-dev
  Development headers and the unversioned linker stub (libckqteec.so) for
  building applications against libckqteec0. Conflicts with optee-client-dev
  due to overlapping header paths; see the "Development Files" section below.

Development Files
-----------------
The mink-optee-client-dev package conflicts with optee-client-dev due to
overlapping header file paths (e.g. /usr/include/pkcs11.h). Only one of the
two -dev packages may be installed at a time.

If you require development headers for the upstream OP-TEE stack, install
optee-client-dev. If you are developing against the Qualcomm QTEE/MinkIPC
stack, install mink-optee-client-dev instead.

To switch between the two:

  # Switch to mink-optee-client-dev
  apt remove optee-client-dev
  apt install mink-optee-client-dev

  # Switch back to optee-client-dev
  apt remove mink-optee-client-dev
  apt install optee-client-dev
